  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 12. Summary (2026-10-13)\n\n**Generic (theta, z), all 256 states [hp 60 digits].** <0|Psi> = lambda^w <0bar^T|Psi> exactly (error < 1e-59). 1/N = sum_{x,y} tauT_y M_yx tau_x equals <PsiL|Psi>/(<0|Psi><PsiL|0bar>) on all 256 states (max relative error < 1e-47; tau, tauT are products of eigenvalues). At finite real twist the right eigenvectors of t^Lambda are not orthogonal, PsiL is not proportional to Psi^T or Psi^dagger (cos 0.12..1) and (R Psi)^T is not a left eigenvector in the companion frame (cos <= 0.06). Exact: |<0|Psi>|^2 = H lambda^w N ||Psi||^2 with H = <Psi^T 0bar><PsiL Psi>/(<PsiL 0bar> Psi^T Psi); H = 1 + O(eps) on the eps-chain: for the two singlets H - 1 = (E/2)(theta_F2 - theta_F1) + O(eps^2) = 3.70 eps (E = 20) and 0.74 eps (E = 4); at pair-periodic theta only the O(eps^2) twist effect remains (max |H - 1| = 0.0088 at eps = 0.1). The exactly Q-based quantity is <0|Psi>^2/<PsiL_*|Psi> = lambda^w/(sum tauT M tau) with PsiL_* normalised by <PsiL_*|0bar> = <0bar^T|Psi>.\n\n**ABJM point (pair-by-pair theta, eps-chain eps = 1/50 ... 1/1600) [exact operators, hp 100-120 digits].** Regularised bra and ket bases (O = {1, t1(u0), W, Z}, K = {1, t1(u0), Wt, Zt}) have rank 256, the exact identities t3(u0) = 0, t2(u0) = t1(u0) t1(thF), t2(thA) = t1(thA) t1(u0), t3(thA + h) = 0 hold for both pairs, the Gram matrix has 3323 nonzeros at every eps. 1/N from eigenvalue data equals the direct overlap ratio on all 28 zero-weight states to < 1e-48 (eps = 1/50), 1e-41 (1/100), 1e-33 (1/200), 1.8e-40 (1/400), 1e-29 (1/800), 1e-32 (1/1600) (accuracy limited by cond(Gram) growth; 100-120 digits). The closed form of <W_a|Psi> matches the direct overlap to < 1e-73 at every eps. Independent python check at eps = 1/100 (exact Fractions, mpmath 80 digits): same |C_dir|, |C_Q|, H on all 28 states, max 1/N error 3e-35.\n\n**Even bridge.** |C_Q|(eps) = |A N_pre W|/sqrt(|B|) with B = sum tauT M tau from eigenvalues only; deg-5 extrapolation over eps = 1/50..1/1600: 0.1581138830084186 vs 1/sqrt(40) = 0.1581138830084190 and 0.2041241452319316 vs 1/sqrt(24) = 0.2041241452319315 (differences 4e-16, 9e-17). Factor limits: (A, W, B) -> (10, 25, 2500000) and (2, 9, 7776), N_pre -> 1, so C = A W/sqrt(B) = 1/sqrt(40) and 1/sqrt(24) exactly. With the data phase (sign of Psi_eps fixed by <Psi_0^data|Psi_eps> > 0) the signed C_direct is -1/sqrt(40), +1/sqrt(24) as in the data.\n\nHousekeeping: the shared kernel was at 2.4 - 7.6 GB MemoryInUse during this session while all `nm*` symbols total < 200 MB (3 MB after the final cleanup); I set `$HistoryLength = 0` once (it blanked the Wolfbook outputs of cells 7-34, which were therefore rerun after restoring `$HistoryLength = 10`).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 13. Reflection structure of the eigenvalue data (python, `checks/session-2026-10-13/norm/abjm_eval2.py`, eps = 1/100, 60 digits)\n\nOn 16 of the 28 zero-weight states (10 real, including both singlets and the top state with |C| = 0.294, and 6 complex ones) the ket data are exactly the bra data of the other pair (1e-47 ... 1e-60): tauA1 = tauF2, tauA2 = tauF1, x1 = x2 = x, wt1 = -w2, wt2 = -w1, yt1 = -y2, yt2 = -y1, i.e. tau1(u) = tau1(c - u), c = thF1 + thF2 + 2h. For these states B depends on the 7 numbers (tauF1, tauF2, x, w1, w2, y1, y2); the 12 remaining states (parity partner triplets with E ~ 630, 597 and 6 complex states) are mapped onto each other by the reflection. Not re-run in the notebook (python).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  }
 ],
